WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.910
In St Louis, the Pruitt-Igoe estate
held 2,740 public-housing flats.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.890
According to Oscar Newman, it never
achieved more than 60 per cent occupancy.

3
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.170
It was torn down, at a loss
of 300 million dollars.

4
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.550
Next door, Carr Square Village, he wrote,

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.330
remained fully occupied and trouble-free.

6
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.870
Same city, next-door estates.

7
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.150
Why did one never fill,
while the other stayed full?

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:33.890
In this mission, you'll test Oscar Newman's
1972 ideas against estates that changed,

9
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.330
in New York and Dayton.

10
00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:41.290
Then you'll weigh his critics' case, and
judge what makes housing sustainable.

11
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.030
Your mission: explain why one St Louis
estate never filled while its neighbour

12
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.150
stayed full.
